{
  "summary": "Validates timeout arguments in the mining interface methods waitNext and waitTipChanged, throwing a std::runtime_error if the timeout is negative or NaN. Updates documentation in interfaces/mining.h and adds functional test coverage verifying remote exceptions over Cap'n Proto IPC.",
  "problem": "IPC callers can supply negative or NaN timeouts to the mining interface. In debug builds, passing negative or NaN values triggers an Assume failure that aborts the node; in release builds, NaN values can bypass comparison clamps and pass invalid deadlines to wait primitives.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author reproduction: 'On debug builds, a negative or NaN timeout fails this check and aborts the node. I reproduced this with a timeout of -1.0.'",
    "Author note on severity: 'I'm not aware of any client that sends these values (sv2-tp, for example, requires an interval of at least one second), so this is hardening against bad input from ipc clients.'"
  ],
